$WW,1$$FG,6$$TX+CX,"Glowie UFOs -- The Story"$$FG$

$TX+CX,"Aliens, BK, Diet Shasta, Glowies, Ohh My! You must help Terry!"$

$FG,10$The Situation$FG$
  The aliens and the glowies are after $FG,12$Terry$FG$, and it is your job to
  help beat them back.  Terry works the ground -- he stays with his car,
  rounding glowies up and keeping his head down.  You fly the only ship that can
  reach the $FG,6$UFOs$FG$, so you provide the air cover.  Patrol the
  planet, gun down the UFOs, and above all keep the UFOs away from Terry.

  Three things keep Terry sharp: food, drink, and his bird.  Keep him fed with
  $FG,10$BK$FG$ and $FG,10$Diet Shasta$FG$, and help him get his lost bird
  back so his mind stays focused.  Don't let the aliens wear him down -- or worse,
  carry him off -- or it is game over.

$FG,10$Terry, the Man You Protect$FG$
  On the run from the glowies Terry is fighting back on the ground as best he
  can with his car.  You are send from the future on a mission to protect him.
  You share any drink or food consumed, both reaping the benefits during your
  battle.  His car shows up as the $FG,12$light-red dot$FG$ on the radar above.  While
  he is free he drives at the nearest glowie to take them out before the aliens
  can help them escape.  Every one he defeats is worth points and counts on the
  $FG,12$TERRY$FG$ tally.  He is racing against the aliens who are trying to save
  them, the faster he moves, the more he can capture, so make sure he gets his
  caffinated Shasta infusion to drive faster when possible.  He also prioritizes
  picking up bonus items that drop for you, so if you need to keep flying and missed
  one, he will pick it up with his car if he drives by it and it will be added to
  your inventory.

  He is initially weaked from lack of BK, Diet Shasta and losing his bird. Because
  of this he is slightly distracted and if a UFO descends on him and grabs
  him, a flashing alert shows $FG,6$"!! TERRY ABDUCTED -- SHOOT THE SHIP !!"$FG$.
  You must shoot that UFO before it reaches the top and Terry drops back to
  the ground unharmed.  Terry is fine, but the scare sends his bird bolting: for
  the rest of that wave the bird flees $FG,10$10% faster$FG$, and if you had
  already brought it home it breaks free and must be caught again.
  Once per wave you you use your ships hyper drive to jump
  to his location to help in an emergency if you are far away.  If you let it carry
  him all the way up it is $FG,12$GAME OVER$FG$ on the spot -- no matter how
  many ships you have left.  Do not let Terry get taken!

$FG,10$The Glowies$FG$
  The $FG,10$glowies$FG$ start on the ground, and they are not on your
  side -- they are helping the aliens.  Each one waits on the surface for a
  $FG,6$UFO$FG$ to drop down and pick it up.  When a UFO carries a glowie all
  the way to space, that craft has completed its primary mission and then turns
  $FG,10$green$FG$ and is on a Kamikazi mission to hunt your ship down and ram you.
  This last-ditch effort comes heading straight at you to ram and destroy your
  ship.  Every glowie that reaches orbit costs you points and puts another
  green killer UFO on your tail.

  So work with him to defeat the glowies by shooting a UFO mid-carry to make it
  drop its glowie back to the ground, and let $FG,12$Terry$FG$ round up the ones
  on the surface before other UFOs can lift them to safety.  A wave only ends once
  every glowie has been accounted for -- captured by $FG,12$Terry$FG$ or carried off by a
  $FG,6$UFO$FG$ -- and every UFO is destroyed.

$FG,10$BK Boost -- the Burger of Power!$FG$
  You and Terry runs on BK burgers.  A $FG,10$BK Boost$FG$ is more than a meal
  -- those burgers have been known to grant super powers.  Spend one with the 
  $FG,11$B$FG$ key and a shockwave of BK power will destroy $FG,10$every alien
  ship on screen at once$FG$.  Save it for a swarm of kamikaze UFOs closing in,
  or to instantly clear a bunch of UFOs landing to fetch glowies (or worse Terry).
  You start with one and earn another at the start of each wave;
  more can drop from tagged enemies.  You can hold up to three.

$FG,10$Diet Shasta -- the Shasta Boost!$FG$
  Terry's other fuel is $FG,10$Diet Shasta$FG$.  A $FG,10$Shasta Boost$FG$ is
  pure caffeine power!  Spend one with the $FG,11$S$FG$ key and for 30 seconds
  $FG,10$both you and Terry$FG$ move much faster.  Use it to sprint across the
  map to a rescue, or to catch Terry's bird before it escapes.  It doesn't just
  help you, Terry's speed also increases.  Diet Shasta can drop randomly from enemies.
  You can hold up to three.

$FG,10$Collecting Boosts$FG$
  Two UFOs each wave arrive carrying a bonus -- a pulsing $FG,11$B$FG$ BK Boost or a
  green $FG,11$S$FG$ Shasta Boost -- which they drop when shot.  The pickup falls to
  the ground: fly low over it to grab it, or let $FG,12$Terry$FG$ drive over it (either
  way it lands in your inventory).  If a carrier UFO reaches the top it turns into a
  kamikaze that still holds the bonus, so shoot it to claim the drop.  You can hold up
  to three of each.

$FG,10$Terry's Bird$FG$
  Terry gets distracted when his bird is lost.  Eventually during a wave a lone bird 
  starts flapping across the middle of the sky, fleeing you along a bobbing path 
  -- watch for its purple dot on the radar.  It flies about as fast as you cruise,
  so catching it takes a real chase; a $FG,10$Shasta Boost$FG$ makes it far easier.
  Fly into it to bring it home.  Recovering the bird gives Terry the last bit of
  peace of mind he needs to focus.  The bird is easily startled, though: if a UFO
  grabs Terry, it bolts -- flying $FG,10$10% faster$FG$ for the rest of the wave,
  and any bird you had already brought home breaks free, so you must chase it down
  again.  $FG,12$Do not shoot the bird$FG$ -- killing it costs you points and
  spoils your shot at the King Terry Bonus for the wave.

$FG,10$King Terry Bonus -- Restoring Terry's Focus$FG$
  Do all three things for Terry in a single wave --
  $FG,10$use a BK Boost$FG$, $FG,10$use a Shasta Boost$FG$, and
  $FG,10$recover his bird$FG$ -- and you crown
  him $FG,10$KING TERRY$FG$.  Letting a UFO grab Terry will not spoil the
  crown by itself, but it scares his bird into flight (see above), so you may
  have to recover the bird a second time to lock the $FG,11$BIRD$FG$ check back
  in.  Well fed and at peace, his divine intellect snaps
  back into focus: for the rest of that wave he becomes
  $FG,10$immune to abduction$FG$.  Any UFO that descends on him is destroyed
  the instant it reaches him, as if you had shot it yourself, and he can no
  longer be carried off.  On top of that you bank a fat
  $FG,10$King Terry Bonus$FG$ at wave's end.  The HUD shows a green check under
  $FG,11$B$FG$, $FG,11$S$FG$, and $FG,11$BIRD$FG$ as you meet each requirement,
  and a crown appears when all three are locked in to show you've achieved it.

$FG,10$The Hyper-Jump Rescue$FG$
  Once per wave, when a UFO has Terry, you can press $FG,11$H$FG$ to
  $FG,10$hyper-jump$FG$ straight to his abductor -- you arrive just to its left,
  facing it.  You get a brief flash of invulnerability on arrival so it is not
  a death trap.  It costs points and only works while Terry is actually being
  taken, so save it for a real emergency you cannot fly to in time.  Watch the
  $FG,10$HYP$FG$ light: green when charged, gray once spent.  It recharges at
  the start of each new wave (not on a respawn), and leaving it unused adds to
  your King Terry bonus.

$FG,10$How the Waves Get Harder$FG$
  Every wave the invasion grows:
  $FG,11$*$FG$ $FG,10$More UFOs.$FG$  UFOs per wave are 4 + 2 per wave,
    climbing until the sky is packed with the maximum of 16 by wave 6.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ $FG,10$Faster enemies.$FG$  From wave 6 on, alien UFOs
    speed up about 3% per wave, up to 1.5x by the low-20s.  The extra speed means
    UFOs close on Terry and glowies faster so you have to react quicker before
    they transform and come to hunt your ship down.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ $FG,10$A faster bird.$FG$  From wave 15 the bird gradually picks
    up speed, up to 1.1x by wave 25 -- late waves you almost always need a
    $FG,10$Shasta Boost$FG$ to catch it and keep your King Terry streak alive.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ $FG,10$Last-ditch ambush.$FG$  From wave 20, when you are down to
    the final stranded glowie an extra Kamikazi randomly spawns.

$FG,10$Wave-Clear Scoring$FG$
  Clearing a wave tallies bonus points for your remaining ships, unused BK Boosts,
  held Shasta Boosts, and the wave number, plus the $FG,10$King Terry Bonus$FG$ if you
  earned it.  The breakdown is shown on the $FG,10$WAVE CLEAR!$FG$ screen -- press
  $FG,11$Space$FG$ to continue to the next wave.  The King Terry Bonus grows with the
  wave level, up to a maximum of $FG,10$5000 points$FG$.

$FG,10$Tips$FG$
  $FG,11$*$FG$ Use a $FG,10$BK Boost$FG$ to wipe out every alien ship you can
    see -- best against swarms or to free Terry instantly if he is in your sight.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ Keep UFOs away from $FG,12$Terry$FG$, especially early in a
    wave, to head off an abduction before it starts.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ Terry's bird is fast and keeps its distance.  Pop a
    $FG,10$Shasta Boost$FG$ and chase it down early, the moment you spot its
    purple dot on the minimap.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ A wave ends when every glowie has been captured by
    $FG,12$Terry$FG$ or the UFOs and every ship is destroyed.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ Sometimes it is smarter to ignore a UFO that is abducting a
    glowie and chase Terry's bird first -- weigh the bird against the loss.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ $FG,12$Terry$FG$ helps you on the ground: he prioritizes grabbing
    item pickups and glowies down there, and every pickup he touches still
    lands in your inventory.  Once you have crowned $FG,10$King Terry$FG$, he can
    no longer be abducted for the rest of the wave, so any UFOs that go for
    him die on contact.
  $FG,11$*$FG$ Saving $FG,12$Terry$FG$ is always worth more than saving a glowie
    -- losing him ends the game outright, while a lost glowie only costs points.

$FG,10$See Also$FG$
